{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In most application scenarios, most beans in the container are "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "singletons"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/factory-scopes.html#beans-factory-scopes-singleton"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". When a singleton bean needs to collaborate with another singleton bean or a non-singleton bean needs to collaborate with another non-singleton bean, you typically handle the dependency by defining one bean as a property of the other. A problem arises when the bean lifecycles are different. Suppose singleton bean A needs to use non-singleton (prototype) bean B, perhaps on each method invocation on A. The container creates the singleton bean A only once, and thus only gets one opportunity to set the properties. The container cannot provide bean A with a new instance of bean B every time one is needed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A solution is to forego some inversion of control. You can "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "make bean A aware of the container"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/factory-nature.html#beans-factory-aware"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " by implementing the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContextAware"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface, and by "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "making a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "getBean(\"B\")"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " call to the container"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/basics.html#beans-factory-client"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " ask for (a typically new) bean B instance every time bean A needs it. The following example shows this approach:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "package fiona.apple;\n\n// Spring-API imports\nimport org.springframework.beans.BeansException;\nimport org.springframework.context.ApplicationContext;\nimport org.springframework.context.ApplicationContextAware;\n\n/**\n * A class that uses a stateful Command-style class to perform\n * some processing.\n */\npublic class CommandManager implements ApplicationContextAware {\n\n\tprivate ApplicationContext applicationContext;\n\n\tpublic Object process(Map commandState) {\n\t\t// grab a new instance of the appropriate Command\n\t\tCommand command = createCommand();\n\t\t// set the state on the (hopefully brand new) Command instance\n\t\tcommand.setState(commandState);\n\t\treturn command.execute();\n\t}\n\n\tprotected Command createCommand() {\n\t\t// notice the Spring API dependency!\n\t\treturn this.applicationContext.getBean(\"command\", Command.class);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void setApplicationContext(\n\t\t\tApplicationContext applicationContext) throws BeansException {\n\t\tthis.applicationContext = applicationContext;\n\t}\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "package fiona.apple\n\n// Spring-API imports\nimport org.springframework.context.ApplicationContext\nimport org.springframework.context.ApplicationContextAware\n\n// A class that uses a stateful Command-style class to perform\n// some processing.\nclass CommandManager : ApplicationContextAware {\n\n\tprivate lateinit var applicationContext: ApplicationContext\n\n\tfun process(commandState: Map<*, *>): Any {\n\t\t// grab a new instance of the appropriate Command\n\t\tval command = createCommand()\n\t\t// set the state on the (hopefully brand new) Command instance\n\t\tcommand.state = commandState\n\t\treturn command.execute()\n\t}\n\n\t// notice the Spring API dependency!\n\tprotected fun createCommand() =\n\t\t\tapplicationContext.getBean(\"command\", Command::class.java)\n\n\toverride fun setApplicationContext(applicationContext: ApplicationContext) {\n\t\tthis.applicationContext = applicationContext\n\t}\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The preceding is not desirable, because the business code is aware of and coupled to the Spring Framework. Method Injection, a somewhat advanced feature of the Spring IoC container, lets you handle this use case cleanly."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You can read more about the motivation for Method Injection in "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "this blog entry"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "link",
                    "target": "https://spring.io/blog/2004/08/06/method-injection/"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "sidebar",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Lookup method injection is the ability of the container to override methods on container-managed beans and return the lookup result for another named bean in the container. The lookup typically involves a prototype bean, as in the scenario described in "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the preceding section"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/dependencies/factory-method-injection.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The Spring Framework implements this method injection by using bytecode generation from the CGLIB library to dynamically generate a subclass that overrides the method."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "For this dynamic subclassing to work, the class that the Spring bean container subclasses cannot be "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "final"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ", and the method to be overridden cannot be "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "final"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ", either."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Unit-testing a class that has an "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "abstract"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " method requires you to subclass the class yourself and to supply a stub implementation of the "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "abstract"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " method."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Concrete methods are also necessary for component scanning, which requires concrete classes to pick up."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "A further key limitation is that lookup methods do not work with factory methods and in particular not with "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "@Bean"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " methods in configuration classes, since, in that case, the container is not in charge of creating the instance and therefore cannot create a runtime-generated subclass on the fly."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the case of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "CommandManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class in the previous code snippet, the Spring container dynamically overrides the implementation of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "createCommand()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "CommandManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class does not have any Spring dependencies, as the reworked example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "package fiona.apple;\n\n// no more Spring imports!\n\npublic abstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tpublic Object process(Object commandState) {\n\t\t// grab a new instance of the appropriate Command interface\n\t\tCommand command = createCommand();\n\t\t// set the state on the (hopefully brand new) Command instance\n\t\tcommand.setState(commandState);\n\t\treturn command.execute();\n\t}\n\n\t// okay... but where is the implementation of this method?\n\tprotected abstract Command createCommand();\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "package fiona.apple\n\n// no more Spring imports!\n\nabstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tfun process(commandState: Any): Any {\n\t\t// grab a new instance of the appropriate Command interface\n\t\tval command = createCommand()\n\t\t// set the state on the (hopefully brand new) Command instance\n\t\tcommand.state = commandState\n\t\treturn command.execute()\n\t}\n\n\t// okay... but where is the implementation of this method?\n\tprotected abstract fun createCommand(): Command\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the client class that contains the method to be injected (the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "CommandManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in this case), the method to be injected requires a signature of the following form:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<public|protected> [abstract] <return-type> theMethodName(no-arguments);"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the method is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "abstract"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the dynamically-generated subclass implements the method. Otherwise, the dynamically-generated subclass overrides the concrete method defined in the original class. Consider the following example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<!-- a stateful bean deployed as a prototype (non-singleton) -->\n<bean id=\"myCommand\" class=\"fiona.apple.AsyncCommand\" scope=\"prototype\">\n\t<!-- inject dependencies here as required -->\n</bean>\n\n<!-- commandManager uses myCommand prototype bean -->\n<bean id=\"commandManager\" class=\"fiona.apple.CommandManager\">\n\t<lookup-method name=\"createCommand\" bean=\"myCommand\"/>\n</bean>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The bean identified as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "commandManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " calls its own "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "createCommand()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method whenever it needs a new instance of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "myCommand"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean. You must be careful to deploy the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "myCommand"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean as a prototype if that is actually what is needed. If it is a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "singleton"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/factory-scopes.html#beans-factory-scopes-singleton"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the same instance of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "myCommand"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean is returned each time."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Alternatively, within the annotation-based component model, you can declare a lookup method through the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Lookup"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public abstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tpublic Object process(Object commandState) {\n\t\tCommand command = createCommand();\n\t\tcommand.setState(commandState);\n\t\treturn command.execute();\n\t}\n\n\t@Lookup(\"myCommand\")\n\tprotected abstract Command createCommand();\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "abstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tfun process(commandState: Any): Any {\n\t\tval command = createCommand()\n\t\tcommand.state = commandState\n\t\treturn command.execute()\n\t}\n\n\t@Lookup(\"myCommand\")\n\tprotected abstract fun createCommand(): Command\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Or, more idiomatically, you can rely on the target bean getting resolved against the declared return type of the lookup method:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public abstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tpublic Object process(Object commandState) {\n\t\tCommand command = createCommand();\n\t\tcommand.setState(commandState);\n\t\treturn command.execute();\n\t}\n\n\t@Lookup\n\tprotected abstract Command createCommand();\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "abstract class CommandManager {\n\n\tfun process(commandState: Any): Any {\n\t\tval command = createCommand()\n\t\tcommand.state = commandState\n\t\treturn command.execute()\n\t}\n\n\t@Lookup\n\tprotected abstract fun createCommand(): Command\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that you should typically declare such annotated lookup methods with a concrete stub implementation, in order for them to be compatible with Spring’s component scanning rules where abstract classes get ignored by default. This limitation does not apply to explicitly registered or explicitly imported bean classes."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Another way of accessing differently scoped target beans is an "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ObjectFactory"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/ "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Provider"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " injection point. See "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Scoped Beans as Dependencies"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "core/beans/factory-scopes.html#beans-factory-scopes-other-injection"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You may also find the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ServiceLocatorFactoryBean"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " (in the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "org.springframework.beans.factory.config"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " package) to be useful."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "beans-factory-lookup-method-injection",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Lookup Method Injection"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A less useful form of method injection than lookup method injection is the ability to replace arbitrary methods in a managed bean with another method implementation. You can safely skip the rest of this section until you actually need this functionality."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "With XML-based configuration metadata, you can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "replaced-method"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " element to replace an existing method implementation with another, for a deployed bean. Consider the following class, which has a method called "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "computeValue"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that we want to override:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public class MyValueCalculator {\n\n\tpublic String computeValue(String input) {\n\t\t// some real code...\n\t}\n\n\t// some other methods...\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "class MyValueCalculator {\n\n\tfun computeValue(input: String): String {\n\t\t// some real code...\n\t}\n\n\t// some other methods...\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A class that implements the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.beans.factory.support.MethodReplacer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface provides the new method definition, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "/**\n * meant to be used to override the existing computeValue(String)\n * implementation in MyValueCalculator\n */\npublic class ReplacementComputeValue implements MethodReplacer {\n\n\tpublic Object reimplement(Object o, Method m, Object[] args) throws Throwable {\n\t\t// get the input value, work with it, and return a computed result\n\t\tString input = (String) args[0];\n\t\t...\n\t\treturn ...;\n\t}\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "/**\n * meant to be used to override the existing computeValue(String)\n * implementation in MyValueCalculator\n */\nclass ReplacementComputeValue : MethodReplacer {\n\n\toverride fun reimplement(obj: Any, method: Method, args: Array<out Any>): Any {\n\t\t// get the input value, work with it, and return a computed result\n\t\tval input = args[0] as String;\n\t\t...\n\t\treturn ...;\n\t}\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The bean definition to deploy the original class and specify the method override would resemble the following example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"myValueCalculator\" class=\"x.y.z.MyValueCalculator\">\n\t<!-- arbitrary method replacement -->\n\t<replaced-method name=\"computeValue\" replacer=\"replacementComputeValue\">\n\t\t<arg-type>String</arg-type>\n\t</replaced-method>\n</bean>\n\n<bean id=\"replacementComputeValue\" class=\"a.b.c.ReplacementComputeValue\"/>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can use one or more "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<arg-type/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " elements within the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<replaced-method/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " element to indicate the method signature of the method being overridden. The signature for the arguments is necessary only if the method is overloaded and multiple variants exist within the class. For convenience, the type string for an argument may be a substring of the fully qualified type name. For example, the following all match "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "java.lang.String"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "java.lang.String\nString\nStr"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Because the number of arguments is often enough to distinguish between each possible choice, this shortcut can save a lot of typing, by letting you type only the shortest string that matches an argument type."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "beans-factory-arbitrary-method-replacement",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Arbitrary Method Replacement"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Method Injection"
      }
    ]
  }
}
